    {
      "actual_eos_at_stop": true,
      "answer_segment": "To determine how old John's youngest son will be in 3 years, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Determine James's current age:**\n   - James is currently twice as old as his sister Dora.\n   - Dora will turn 12 in 3 years, so her current age is \\(12 - 3 = 9\\) years.\n   - Therefore, James's current age is \\(2 \\times 9 = 18\\) years.\n\n2. **Determine John's current age:**\n   - John is currently 19 years old.\n\n3. **Determine the age of John's youngest son:**\n   - John's youngest son was born when John was 32 years old.\n   - The age difference between John and his youngest son is \\(32 - 19 = 13\\) years.\n   - Therefore, John's youngest son is currently \\(19 + 13 = 32\\) years old.\n\n4. **Determine the age of John's youngest son in 3 years:**\n   - John's youngest son is currently 32 years old.\n   - In 3 years, he will be \\(32 + 3 = 35\\) years old.\n\nThus, the age of John's youngest son in 3 years will be \\(\\boxed{35}\\).",
      "boundary_offset": null,
