    {
      "actual_eos_at_stop": true,
      "answer_segment": "To determine how many more oranges Ana will have peeled than Jane after an hour, we need to calculate the number of oranges each can peel in that time and then find the difference.\n\nFirst, let's determine how many oranges each can peel in one minute:\n- Ana peels 3 oranges per minute.\n- Jane peels 4 oranges per minute.\n\nNext, we calculate how many oranges each can peel in one hour (60 minutes):\n- Ana peels \\(3 \\text{ oranges/minute} \\times 60 \\text{ minutes} = 180 \\text{ oranges}\\).\n- Jane peels \\(4 \\text{ oranges/minute} \\times 60 \\text{ minutes} = 240 \\text{ oranges}\\).\n\nNow, we find the difference in the number of oranges peeled by Ana and Jane after an hour:\n\\[240 \\text{ oranges} - 180 \\text{ oranges} = 60 \\text{ oranges}.\\]\n\nTherefore, after an hour, Ana will have peeled \\(\\boxed{60}\\) more oranges than Jane.",
