      "answer_segment": "To determine how many pizza slices each person can have, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of pizza slices.\n2. Determine how many people are sharing the pizzas.\n3. Divide the total number of slices by the number of people.\n\nFirst, we calculate the total number of pizza slices. Since each pizza is cut into 8 slices and there are 7 pizzas, we multiply the number of pizzas by the number of slices per pizza:\n\\[ 7 \\text{ pizzas} \\times 8 \\text{ slices per pizza} = 56 \\text{ slices} \\]\n\nNext, we determine how many people are sharing the pizzas. Henry and his 3 friends make a total of 4 people:\n\\[ 1 \\text{ (Henry)} + 3 \\text{ (friends)} = 4 \\text{ people} \\]\n\nNow, we divide the total number of slices by the number of people to find out how many slices each person can have:\n\\[ 56 \\text{ slices} \\div 4 \\text{ people} = 14 \\text{ slices per person} \\]\n\nTherefore, each person can have \\(\\boxed{14}\\) slices.",
